# Independent review: status observations in the receipt journal

Verdict: no blocking finding in the reviewed local status-history scope. Exact source snapshots match commit c7de36f.

Reviewed the diff from 86b124c, journal.py, six real-Git tests and the README against chapter 15's observation/receipt/intent association and fail-closed reconciliation requirements. The shared _created helper retains full preceding-intent identity and original receipt validation. status_history finds the latest contiguous observation suffix, revalidates the receipt and every complete event identity, validates the evidence version/fields and request endpoint, decodes the original response bytes and recomputes the typed observation. Only a pending result permits another observation. record_status checks the expected head and delegates the final old-head CAS to journal append; size limits apply before changing the ref.

Independent execution: all six receipt/status journal tests passed normally and with Python -O; raw logs and commands.json preserve those results. These include the previous creation bridge regressions, exact status-byte reload, rejection after success, wrong request URLs and a forged generic-storage observation. An additional real-Git probe uses RecoveryIntent and separately tests failed, future/unknown and succeeded terminal responses. For each, record_status rejects the next observation without changing the head; adding that next event through generic storage causes status_history to reject the forged sequence on reload. probe.py and probe-results.json retain this independent evidence.

The README correctly describes journal order rather than wall-clock ordering and does not authenticate caller-supplied raw responses. Actual request attribution is the transport/publisher's responsibility. Generic {} intent storage is not deployment authorization. A stored succeed is not proof of current public identity, public smoke, protected-remote durability or immutable LKG. No live API call, remote journal push, publisher state transition or LKG promotion was performed. The reviewer made no implementation edits.
